<title>GERMANY: VW details grp vehicle sales, output data.</title>
<headline>VW details grp vehicle sales, output data.</headline>
<dateline>WOLFSBURG, Germany 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German carmaker Volkswagen AG gave the following breakdown of its vehicle deliveries, sales and production as well as group workforce for the first six months of 1997.</p>
<p>    Group deliveries to customers	  2,193,518 vs 1,995,560</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>    --Domestic				   508,704   vs 516,413</p>
<p>    --International			    1,684,814 vs 1,479,147</p>
<p>    Group vehicle sales			2,185,383 vs 2,104,502</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>    --Domestic				   511,088   vs 515,142</p>
<p>    --International			    1,674,295 vs 1,499,360</p>
<p>    Group vehicle production		 2,207,408 vs 2,039,544</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>    --Domestic				   832,703   vs 827,129</p>
<p>    --International			    1,374,705 vs 1,212,415</p>
<p>    Group workforce			    270,211   vs 260,811</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>    --Domestic				   141,929   vs 137,769</p>
<p>    --International			    128,282   vs 123,042</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German carmaker is Volkswagen AG, which sells vehicles under the Volkswagen, Audi, Skoda and SEAT brands.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
